TEXT -112 -16 Left 2 !.tran 0 500m 0 0.1m
TEXT -112 -24 Left 2 !.param tdv=1 tdt=1 fn1=50
TEXT -112 208 Left 5 ;Computation of active power P = Urms*Irms*cos(phi)\nComputation of reactive power Q = Urms*Irms*sin(phi)\nComputation of apparent power S = sqrt(P*P+Q*Q) or Urms*Irms\nNOTE: phi=phiu-phii\n \nHINT: Get Urms, Irms, phi from FFT-viewer:\n===========================\n1) Simulate the circuit\n2) Click (Activate) the waveformviewerwindow\n3) Choose View/FFT from the menu above\n4) Choose V(in1) by clicking for voltage of circuit one\n5) Choose specify a time range\n6) Choose 40ms to 500ms (always full sinuswaves 460ms/20ms=23x)\n7) Choose binomial smoothing 1 point\n8) Right click on left scale\n9) Change db to linear\n10) Write down Urms (57.7V)\n11) Right click on right scale\n12) Enable this axis \n13) Zoom to about 50Hz\n14) Write down phase(Urms)=phiu at 50Hz (-90°)\n15) Choose Ix(U2:L1_1) by clicking for current of circuit one\n16) Do the same from 5) to 14) IRMS=183.7 phii=-180°\n17) Now you can compute Q1 in the waveformviewer Urms*Irms*sin(phiu-phii)=+10.600kVAr -> 57.7*183.7*sin(-90+180)\n18) Do the same for circuit2 (Irms,Urms,phiu=same as circuit one, phii=0°) Q2=Urms*Irms*sin(-90°)=-10.600kVar ->  (57.7*183.7*sin(-90-0))\n19) and circuit3 (Irms,Urms,phiu the same) phii=-90° Q3=Urms*Irms*sin(0°)= 0 P3=Urms*Irms*cos(0°)=10.600kW -> 57.7*183.7*cos(-90+90)
TEXT -112 0 Left 2 ;circuit one
TEXT -112 64 Left 2 ;circuit two
TEXT -112 128 Left 2 ;circuit three
TEXT 104 0 Left 2 ;Q=10.6kVAr
TEXT 104 64 Left 2 ;Q=-10.6kVAr
TEXT 104 128 Left 2 ;P=10.6kW
TEXT 296 72 Left 5 ;HINT: This computations can also be done if higher harmonics\nare present: See examplefile in this folder
TEXT 96 280 Left 5 ;NOTE: angle = atan(im(X)/re(x))
